[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://ck34knquhucbv" path="res://engine/gamemaster/effects_controller/fx_endless/fx_endless.gd" id="1_fxe"]
[ext_resource type="ArrayMesh" uid="uid://dlvkhs8kmckpi" path="res://assets/fx/resources/icosphere_smoke.tres" id="2_smoke"]

; THE SPORE CLOUD, IN THE MYCONID'S OWN COLOURS. The author playtested SP2.5 Task 5 and said "Cloud
; releases correctly, though it could use with a a pink tinge to match the frames color scheme."
;
; THIS FILE IS res://content/fx_endless/gear/aura/fxe_nanites.tscn WITH ONE PROPERTY CHANGED - the
; ParticleProcessMaterial's `color`, vanilla's neutral grey at fxe_nanites.tscn:30. Every curve,
; velocity, damping, scale, emission extent, particle count, lifetime, speed and the mesh are
; vanilla's numbers, copied so a reader can diff the two files and find exactly one line of physics
; unchanged and one line of colour changed. (The two scenes are not byte-identical outside that: the
; per-node `unique_id=` attributes vanilla carries are omitted here, as they are in our own
; Reag-ThyHubris/res/content/fx_endless/gear/fxe_plague_fog.tscn, and this file has no `uid=` on its
; [gd_scene] line for the same reason the mod's .tres files have none.)
;
; ================= WHY A NEW FILE AND NOT AN EDIT OR AN EXTENSION =================
;
; THE VANILLA SCENE IS BASE GAME AND IS SHARED. fxe_nanites.tscn has exactly one other user in the
; tree - content/gear/horus/systems/ms_hive_drone/deployable/mt_hive_drone.tres:24, the Hive Drone's
; own burst-2 nanite zone. (It is NOT also the Swarm Body's, which an earlier note claimed:
; ms_swarm_body.tres:22 draws fxe_swarm_body.tscn.) A .tscn_ext.gd on the nanite path would therefore
; recolour the Hive Drone's cloud too, which is not ours to repaint, and editing the vanilla file
; itself is off limits outright.
;
; AND IT MUST NOT SIT AT THE VANILLA PATH. The mod overlay maps res/... onto res:// by stripping the
; prefix (LancerTacticsMod.get_vanilla_path, lancer_tactics_mod.gd:42-46), so a file at
; res/content/fx_endless/gear/aura/fxe_nanites.tscn would REPLACE vanilla's scene rather than add
; one. This path is new, so it is additive: nothing vanilla changes and the Hive Drone keeps its grey.
;
; THE PATH STILL HAS TO BE UNDER res/content/ FOR THE ENGINE TO FIND IT AT ALL. FxEndless ids are
; resolved through ContentLibrary.fxendless_library (fx_endless.gd:84 into content_library.gd:215-217),
; which is filled by globbing files whose NAME begins with 'fxe_' and which contain '.tscn'
; (content_library.gd:319-321, the prefix at :108), over a file list that is mod-inclusive only
; because get_all_files_recursive_mod_inclusive appends a mod's own paths when their VANILLA mapping
; begins with the scanned directory (content_library.gd:419-433, the test at :426). res://content is
; that directory (:4), and this file's vanilla mapping is under it. A frame-folder location is also
; what the rest of this Kit does, and it has a worked precedent in our other mod:
; Reag-ThyHubris/res/content/frames/horus/mf_banshee/cp_the_keening/tear/fxe_void_tear.tscn.
;
; THE ID IS THE BASENAME, `fxe_fungal_network` - FxEndless.get_id_from_scene returns
; resource_path.get_file().get_basename() (fx_endless.gd:93-96) and Passive.get_fxe_id just forwards
; to it (passive.gd:31). So RENAMING THIS FILE CHANGES THE ID, and a name ContentLibrary has no entry
; for is a silent no-draw: get_fxendless_path logs an error and returns '' (content_library.gd:215-219),
; create_from_id then hands back null and reconstruct_add appends nothing (fx_endless.gd:84-91 into
; fx_endless_controller.gd:72-74). spec/test_fungal_network.gd pins the id for that reason.

