; ================= THE ONE LINE THIS FILE EXISTS FOR, AND HOW TO RE-DERIVE IT =================
;
; A STARTING VALUE, NOT A FINISHED ONE. Nobody can judge a particle haze from a spec - every test in
; spec/test_fungal_network.gd section H would stay green against any colour at all - so this is a
; defensible first guess the author is expected to nudge on screen. Changing it is this one line.
;
; THE ARITHMETIC, from mf_myconid.tres's Resource_colorscheme. base_0 is the scheme's grey
; (mf_myconid.tres:21) and carries no hue, so the tinge comes from the two that do:
;
;   base_1 = Color(0.39662534, 0.14987248, 0.37463072, 1)   deep purple-magenta   (mf_myconid.tres:22)
;   base_2 = Color(0.8009519,  0.45614117, 0.42966625, 1)   dusty rose            (mf_myconid.tres:23)
;
;   1. blend them 50/50, channel by channel, in the same sRGB space the .tscn stores:
;        mid = (0.59878862, 0.30300683, 0.40214849)      mean of the three channels = 0.43464798
;   2. vanilla's haze is neutral grey 0.26666668 on all three channels (fxe_nanites.tscn:30), so its
;      channel mean IS 0.26666668. Scale the blend to match it:
;        k = 0.26666668 / 0.43464798 = 0.6135233
;   3. mid * k = (0.3673708, 0.1859017, 0.2467275), whose three channels sum to exactly 0.8 and whose
;      mean is therefore 0.26666667 - vanilla's weight, kept to seven places.
;
; WHAT THAT BUYS: a TINGE rather than a repaint. Hue lands at ~340 degrees (rose-pink, between the
; scheme's magenta and its rose) with saturation ~0.49, and the haze reads at the same average
; intensity vanilla's grey did, so the cloud does not suddenly become the loudest thing on the board.
;
; TWO ALTERNATIVES WEIGHED AND NOT TAKEN:
;
;   - NORMALISING TO REC.709 LUMINANCE (0.2126 R + 0.7152 G + 0.0722 B) instead of to the channel
;     mean gives (0.42804, 0.21660, 0.28747). That is the more perceptually honest "same brightness",
;     since this colour's green - the channel the eye weighs most - is the one the blend drops. It
;     was rejected as a STARTING point only because it is the brighter, louder of the two, and the
;     request was for a tinge; if the author wants the cloud to carry the same apparent weight as
;     vanilla's rather than the same average channel, that triple is the one to paste in.
;   - LETTING THE ENGINE COLOUR IT. Setting energy_color_override = true on the root (fx_endless.gd:19)
;     makes sync_to_ticket push the UNIT's own base_2 into every child's process_material each time
;     the ticket syncs (fx_endless.gd:72-74 into apply_color_recursive at :49-60). Vanilla uses it on
;     eight scenes and gavstarb-horus_alts_1st_party's Hecatoncheires nanobots do too, so it is a real
;     option. Rejected for THIS cloud on two counts. It does not read the FRAME's scheme: it reads
;     unit.core.token_customization.colors, which TokenCore.create seeds as a DUPLICATE of the frame's
;     default_color_scheme (token_core.gd:28-33) and which the player then repaints freely - so the
;     tie to "the frame's colour scheme" is only as good as the paint job. And base_2 undiluted is
;     Color(0.8009519, 0.45614117, 0.42966625) - a channel mean of 0.562, more than double vanilla's
;     haze - which is a repaint, not a tinge. It also writes through a process_material that
;     instances of one PackedScene share unless resource_local_to_scene is set, which nothing here
;     sets, so the last unit to sync would be colouring everyone else's cloud as well.
color = Color(0.3673708, 0.1859017, 0.2467275, 1)

; lock_height_to = 3 is FxEndless.LOCK_TO.SURFACE - "sets to surface elevation (terrain blocks +
; setpieces + obstructing units)" (fx_endless.gd:11-18, the export at :18). It is vanilla's value on
; fxe_nanites.tscn:34 and it is what puts the haze ON THE GROUND rather than at the token's centre,
; which is the LOCK_TO.UNIT default. That is the whole reason Task 5 picked this scene to copy, so it
; is carried over unchanged; position_fxe reads it at fx_endless_controller.gd:123-134.
[node name="Fxe" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_fxe")
lock_height_to = 3

[node name="SporeCloud" type="GPUParticles3D" parent="."]
amount = 40
lifetime = 1.5
speed_scale = 0.5
randomness = 0.6
process_material = SubResource("ParticleProcessMaterial_spores")
draw_pass_1 = ExtResource("2_smoke")
